WEBVTT

1
00:00:41.875 --> 00:00:42.956
<i>Can't you remember?</i>

2
00:00:43.043 --> 00:00:45.000
<i>No, I can't...</i>

3
00:00:46.880 --> 00:00:48.541
<i>So, you can't remember...</i>

4
00:00:52.344 --> 00:00:53.425
<i>Kill him.</i>

5
00:01:02.688 --> 00:01:05.476
Why are you sweating?

6
00:01:05.983 --> 00:01:07.894
Are you okay?

7
00:01:09.486 --> 00:01:10.476
Mom?

8
00:01:10.696 --> 00:01:11.652
Yes, Jin-seok.

9
00:01:11.738 --> 00:01:14.275
Did you have a nightmare, son?

10
00:01:14.950 --> 00:01:15.985
Dad?

11
00:01:16.660 --> 00:01:18.651
Should've listened to your big bro.

12
00:01:18.704 --> 00:01:20.945
I told you to sleep early
for moving day.

13
00:01:21.957 --> 00:01:22.947
Bro?

14
00:01:23.959 --> 00:01:28.078
He was so excited to move,
he didn't sleep all night.

15
00:01:29.756 --> 00:01:31.372
We're almost there.

16
00:01:31.383 --> 00:01:33.374
What should we eat for lunch?

17
00:01:33.677 --> 00:01:36.294
Black bean noodles, of course!

18
00:01:37.264 --> 00:01:38.925
Great idea!

19
00:01:58.535 --> 00:02:00.117
<i>Our new house.</i>

20
00:02:01.204 --> 00:02:06.620
<i>I've never seen it before, but
somehow it feels familiar.</i>

21
00:02:08.045 --> 00:02:14.587
<i>As if I stood here in the past
and saw the house before...</i>

22
00:02:14.676 --> 00:02:16.166
<i>Why do I get that feeling?</i>

23
00:02:16.303 --> 00:02:17.589
Do you like it?

24
00:02:21.141 --> 00:02:24.429
Is it the house you dreamed of?

25
00:02:31.151 --> 00:02:35.190
<i>My brother topped his
class all through school.</i>

26
00:02:35.906 --> 00:02:39.570
<i>He graduated from the most
prestigious university.</i>

27
00:02:40.869 --> 00:02:44.988
<i>He was remarkably talented
in everything since he was young.</i>

28
00:02:48.085 --> 00:02:52.875
<i>He had a strong competitive spirit
and was very athletic.</i>

29
00:02:53.715 --> 00:02:54.705
Yes!

30
00:02:55.467 --> 00:03:00.587
<i>He was also handy and good
at fixing everything.</i>

31
00:03:02.391 --> 00:03:06.760
<i>He never smoked, drank, or
said anything indecent.</i>

32
00:03:07.145 --> 00:03:10.058
<i>He was a logical and
eloquent speaker.</i>

33
00:03:10.899 --> 00:03:14.017
<i>He was the awe and envy of everyone.</i>

34
00:03:15.570 --> 00:03:18.232
<i>Of course, I liked my brother too.</i>

35
00:03:19.157 --> 00:03:20.022
<i>No.</i>

36
00:03:20.242 --> 00:03:21.824
<i>I respected him.</i>

37
00:03:23.995 --> 00:03:28.831
<i>To a high school repeater with
chronic nervous breakdowns,</i>

38
00:03:28.917 --> 00:03:32.410
<i>my brother was my pride and joy.</i>

39
00:03:32.504 --> 00:03:33.585
Yu-seok!

40
00:03:34.464 --> 00:03:36.455
I'll take that, Mom.

41
00:03:39.720 --> 00:03:44.385
<i>Though his left leg became
impaired in an accident last year,</i>

42
00:03:45.100 --> 00:03:50.095
<i>he's still the perfect
hero to my family and I.</i>

43
00:03:52.190 --> 00:03:54.272
- Careful.
- Where to?

44
00:03:54.276 --> 00:03:56.893
- There, please.
- Okay.

45
00:04:00.031 --> 00:04:03.524
- Beside the post, please.
- Sure.

46
00:04:06.538 --> 00:04:09.155
- Be careful, please.
- Yes.

47
00:04:12.711 --> 00:04:14.042
Where do you want this?

48
00:04:14.296 --> 00:04:17.414
I'll take those books.

49
00:04:21.011 --> 00:04:22.126
There.

50
00:04:40.572 --> 00:04:41.482
Bro?

51
00:04:42.115 --> 00:04:43.856
We're sharing this room?

52
00:04:44.242 --> 00:04:45.778
You didn't hear?

53
00:04:46.119 --> 00:04:49.703
The owner before us left some
stuff in the small room.

54
00:04:51.500 --> 00:04:54.117
So we can't use that room ever?

55
00:04:54.211 --> 00:04:55.872
I'm not sure.

56
00:04:56.671 --> 00:05:00.915
He begged and Dad couldn't say no.

57
00:05:01.551 --> 00:05:03.007
Won't be long.

58
00:05:04.930 --> 00:05:07.297
Why? You hate sharing a room with me?

59
00:05:08.183 --> 00:05:09.173
Yup.

60
00:05:09.518 --> 00:05:12.135
I thought so. I knew it.

61
00:05:13.271 --> 00:05:14.181
Kidding.

62
00:05:14.272 --> 00:05:15.808
Just curious.

63
00:05:16.233 --> 00:05:18.850
- Yu-seok!
- Yes, Mom!

64
00:05:18.985 --> 00:05:21.317
Come down and help me?

65
00:05:25.826 --> 00:05:26.736
Why you!

66
00:05:27.077 --> 00:05:29.569
Not the head! It kills brain cells!

67
00:05:30.121 --> 00:05:31.327
No way!

68
00:05:37.337 --> 00:05:38.668
- Excuse me.
- Yes?

69
00:05:38.797 --> 00:05:40.333
Where do you want this?

70
00:05:40.340 --> 00:05:43.708
- By the bed, please.
- Okay.

71
00:05:47.305 --> 00:05:49.296
- Are you all right?
- Yes.

72
00:05:51.226 --> 00:05:53.012
Thank you.

73
00:05:53.353 --> 00:05:55.344
It's our stuff anyway.

74
00:05:57.357 --> 00:06:01.021
That man is your older brother?

75
00:06:01.736 --> 00:06:02.817
Yes. Why?

76
00:06:04.239 --> 00:06:05.650
Really?

77
00:06:08.326 --> 00:06:10.112
Yes. We don't look alike.

78
00:06:10.203 --> 00:06:12.820
Then how old is your brother?

79
00:06:12.914 --> 00:06:14.404
- Why?
- Mister?

80
00:06:15.292 --> 00:06:17.329
Someone's looking for
you in the kitchen.

81
00:06:17.419 --> 00:06:18.955
Okay.

82
00:06:29.931 --> 00:06:31.968
I'm exhausted!

83
00:06:35.770 --> 00:06:36.680
Dinner time!

84
00:06:36.771 --> 00:06:39.809
Jin-seok? Like the house?

85
00:06:40.108 --> 00:06:41.519
Yes, Mom.

86
00:06:41.735 --> 00:06:43.396
Really? You sure?

87
00:06:43.987 --> 00:06:46.775
Yes, he says he loves it.

88
00:06:46.990 --> 00:06:48.776
Except sharing the room.

89
00:06:50.118 --> 00:06:51.108
Hey!

90
00:06:51.119 --> 00:06:52.405
It won't be long.

91
00:06:52.412 --> 00:06:54.949
He said he'll take his
stuff in a month.

92
00:06:54.956 --> 00:06:57.618
I was just kidding, Dad.

93
00:06:58.335 --> 00:07:00.326
No, you weren't!

94
00:07:01.296 --> 00:07:02.502
Yes, I was.

95
00:07:02.839 --> 00:07:03.829
It's good.

96
00:07:03.840 --> 00:07:08.129
You can ask your brother
questions as you study.

97
00:07:08.720 --> 00:07:12.338
Dad? Did he say what's in the room?

98
00:07:12.474 --> 00:07:15.057
Probably stuff he used.

99
00:07:16.061 --> 00:07:18.052
What kind of stuff?

100
00:07:18.396 --> 00:07:20.854
I have to warn you.

101
00:07:21.191 --> 00:07:23.057
Don't ever go into that room.

102
00:07:23.068 --> 00:07:26.277
He begged me not to look inside.

103
00:07:28.198 --> 00:07:30.860
Jin-seok? Are you taking your pills?

104
00:07:31.076 --> 00:07:33.488
- Of course, Dad.
- Good.

105
00:07:41.252 --> 00:07:42.538
What's that sound?

106
00:07:44.005 --> 00:07:44.995
What sound?

107
00:07:45.173 --> 00:07:46.504
It came from upstairs.

108
00:07:47.050 --> 00:07:49.041
Sounded like something heavy dropped.

109
00:07:49.135 --> 00:07:50.546
Wasn't it the thunder?

110
00:07:50.595 --> 00:07:52.506
No, it wasn't the thunder.

111
00:07:53.014 --> 00:07:55.005
Isn't the small room above us?

112
00:07:55.308 --> 00:07:57.299
Yes, it is.

113
00:07:58.520 --> 00:08:00.102
Wasn't it the thunder?

114
00:08:00.438 --> 00:08:01.678
I don't think so.

115
00:08:04.359 --> 00:08:06.350
- It was the thunder.
- Right.

116
00:08:07.404 --> 00:08:08.519
I guess.

117
00:08:09.322 --> 00:08:11.780
The weather calls for
heavy rain till morning.

118
00:08:12.742 --> 00:08:15.825
Good thing it's raining
after we moved in.

119
00:08:16.538 --> 00:08:17.653
That's right.

120
00:08:17.872 --> 00:08:20.534
- We're really lucky.
- I know.

121
00:08:50.155 --> 00:08:51.611
Don't worry.

122
00:08:52.782 --> 00:08:53.772
About what?

123
00:08:55.535 --> 00:08:57.367
You'll pass this time.

124
00:08:59.247 --> 00:09:01.409
This house has good vibes.

125
00:09:08.173 --> 00:09:09.379
Man.

126
00:09:10.800 --> 00:09:12.165
I'd better sleep.

127
00:10:49.315 --> 00:10:51.477
<i>Don't ever go into that room.</i>

128
00:11:06.624 --> 00:11:07.580
Bro!

129
00:11:07.834 --> 00:11:08.915
What are you doing?

130
00:11:09.502 --> 00:11:11.493
I heard something in here.

131
00:11:12.881 --> 00:11:15.464
- Heard what?
- A strange noise.

132
00:11:23.725 --> 00:11:24.681
Hear it?

133
00:11:24.684 --> 00:11:26.516
I don't hear anything.

134
00:11:27.478 --> 00:11:28.309
Really?

135
00:11:34.777 --> 00:11:37.394
But I swear I heard something!

136
00:11:37.614 --> 00:11:39.651
You don't want to study, huh?

137
00:11:39.657 --> 00:11:42.615
No, that's not it.
I heard something strange.

138
00:11:42.869 --> 00:11:46.282
Okay, okay. Going for
a walk should help.

139
00:11:46.456 --> 00:11:48.788
What? It's raining outside.

140
00:11:49.209 --> 00:11:50.950
We'll take umbrellas.

141
00:11:52.378 --> 00:11:55.211
There's a park up the hill.

142
00:11:59.510 --> 00:12:01.592
The rain is refreshing.

143
00:12:04.682 --> 00:12:05.547
Bro?

144
00:12:06.684 --> 00:12:07.674
Hmm?

145
00:12:09.395 --> 00:12:10.385
Thanks.

146
00:12:12.607 --> 00:12:13.642
For what?

147
00:12:14.734 --> 00:12:15.565
You know.

148
00:12:15.568 --> 00:12:18.105
Why you little...

149
00:12:26.788 --> 00:12:27.778
Hello?

150
00:12:29.582 --> 00:12:30.572
Yes, Dad.

151
00:12:31.626 --> 00:12:33.617
We stepped out for a walk.

152
00:12:35.588 --> 00:12:36.749
Yes.

153
00:12:36.965 --> 00:12:38.171
Oh, that?

154
00:12:41.719 --> 00:12:43.710
I'll go down and find it.

155
00:12:44.764 --> 00:12:45.879
Bye.

156
00:12:47.058 --> 00:12:48.514
- That was Dad?
- Yup.

157
00:12:48.601 --> 00:12:51.639
He needs one of my books now.

158
00:12:53.064 --> 00:12:55.522
I'll be right back. Wait here.

159
00:12:55.733 --> 00:12:57.440
- I'll go with you.
- It's okay.

160
00:12:57.443 --> 00:12:58.979
I won't be long.

161
00:12:59.237 --> 00:13:00.477
Wait here.

162
00:13:01.197 --> 00:13:02.403
Okay.

163
00:13:46.784 --> 00:13:47.774
Who are you?

164
00:14:11.517 --> 00:14:12.507
Get him!

165
00:14:21.694 --> 00:14:22.684
Bro!

166
00:14:23.112 --> 00:14:23.943
Stay still!

167
00:14:27.158 --> 00:14:28.023
Bro!

168
00:14:34.624 --> 00:14:36.160
Bro!

169
00:14:51.391 --> 00:14:53.223
07J 8911.

170
00:14:53.810 --> 00:14:55.175
07J 8911.

171
00:14:55.561 --> 00:14:56.972
07J 8911.

172
00:15:04.862 --> 00:15:05.852
Jin-seok!

173
00:15:06.906 --> 00:15:07.987
What's wrong?

174
00:15:08.241 --> 00:15:09.527
It's terrible.

175
00:15:09.867 --> 00:15:12.074
Yu-seok's been abducted.

176
00:15:13.121 --> 00:15:14.828
- No!
- Jin-seok!

177
00:15:15.873 --> 00:15:16.863
Hey!

178
00:15:17.583 --> 00:15:19.995
Jin-seok! Wake up!

179
00:15:20.545 --> 00:15:22.127
Oh no!

180
00:15:42.859 --> 00:15:43.599
<i>Kill him.</i>

181
00:15:48.781 --> 00:15:50.772
Jin-seok? Are you okay?

182
00:15:53.077 --> 00:15:54.112
Mom?

183
00:15:54.954 --> 00:15:57.321
Yes, it's me. Are you okay?

184
00:16:01.002 --> 00:16:02.993
Where's Yu-seok?

185
00:16:03.921 --> 00:16:06.458
He's not back yet.

186
00:16:07.258 --> 00:16:09.215
- Did you report him missing?
- Yes.

187
00:16:09.218 --> 00:16:12.210
Police will be here soon
to ask you what happened.

188
00:16:20.313 --> 00:16:23.931
Do you remember any
of the men's faces?

189
00:16:25.818 --> 00:16:26.808
No.

190
00:16:27.612 --> 00:16:30.980
It was raining hard
and it happened so fast.

191
00:16:31.699 --> 00:16:33.406
I didn't see their faces.

192
00:16:35.286 --> 00:16:37.823
But I definitely saw
the license plate.

193
00:16:38.080 --> 00:16:40.367
07J 8911. A black van.

194
00:16:41.125 --> 00:16:42.957
How frustrating.

195
00:16:43.002 --> 00:16:44.868
That plate doesn't exist.

196
00:16:45.421 --> 00:16:48.083
No, it was definitely 07J 8911.

197
00:16:48.299 --> 00:16:51.462
We checked all black
vans in the country.

198
00:16:51.636 --> 00:16:53.718
No, all cars! The plate doesn't exist.

199
00:16:53.971 --> 00:16:57.214
- No, sir! I saw it!
- Look.

200
00:16:58.017 --> 00:17:02.762
We checked for similar numbers,
but there was no black van.

201
00:17:04.649 --> 00:17:09.268
It was really raining hard that night.

202
00:17:09.278 --> 00:17:11.440
You could've seen wrong.

203
00:17:14.825 --> 00:17:17.192
You take pills for nervous breakdowns?

204
00:17:17.662 --> 00:17:20.996
No! It was definitely 07J 8911!
A black van!

205
00:17:21.165 --> 00:17:22.451
Jin-seok...

206
00:17:22.667 --> 00:17:24.374
Could we stop for today?

207
00:17:25.169 --> 00:17:29.458
My son is not well.
I think he's very startled.

208
00:17:30.007 --> 00:17:31.088
Okay, then.

209
00:17:33.636 --> 00:17:38.051
<i>Then it was hell waiting
with no end in sight.</i>

210
00:17:48.943 --> 00:17:49.557
<i>One day...</i>

211
00:17:51.070 --> 00:17:52.060
<i>Two...</i>

212
00:17:54.699 --> 00:17:56.030
<i>A week...</i>

213
00:17:58.286 --> 00:18:03.952
<i>After two weeks, the
police lost interest.</i>

214
00:18:04.417 --> 00:18:10.003
<i>My parents and I became
more and more worried.</i>

215
00:18:50.087 --> 00:18:50.701
<i>Kill him.</i>

216
00:18:53.966 --> 00:18:56.924
<i>The man was in my dream every night.</i>

217
00:18:57.511 --> 00:19:01.379
<i>He seems familiar, but I
don't know who he is.</i>

218
00:19:02.099 --> 00:19:05.683
<i>He's in utter pain in my dreams.</i>

219
00:21:38.130 --> 00:21:44.297
<i>19 days after being abducted,</i>

220
00:21:45.721 --> 00:21:47.132
<i>my brother came back.</i>

221
00:21:53.771 --> 00:22:00.359
<i>But he had no memory of what
happened during the 19 days.</i>

222
00:22:04.240 --> 00:22:06.197
Do you remember anything at all?

223
00:22:06.367 --> 00:22:09.359
<i>He had dissociative amnesia.</i>

224
00:22:10.412 --> 00:22:15.828
<i>He erased the painful
memories himself.</i>

225
00:22:17.211 --> 00:22:24.379
<i>The only way to bring back
his memory was waiting.</i>

226
00:22:30.975 --> 00:22:32.181
Sleeping?

227
00:22:34.770 --> 00:22:35.760
No.

228
00:22:37.857 --> 00:22:39.643
We were really worried.

229
00:22:42.403 --> 00:22:43.939
I'm so sorry.

230
00:22:44.989 --> 00:22:48.277
No, I'm the one who's sorry.

231
00:22:51.829 --> 00:22:52.864
Sleep tight.

232
00:22:56.500 --> 00:22:58.537
You too.

233
00:24:20.626 --> 00:24:23.288
<i>EAT THE SOUP I MADE.
DON'T ORDER NOODLES! - MOM</i>

234
00:24:45.901 --> 00:24:47.187
What are you doing?

235
00:24:47.903 --> 00:24:49.018
Hi, bro.

236
00:24:50.406 --> 00:24:51.396
It's nothing.

237
00:24:51.490 --> 00:24:52.651
Slept well?

238
00:24:54.368 --> 00:24:56.450
I'm hungry. Let's eat.

239
00:25:02.334 --> 00:25:03.449
It's so good!

240
00:25:05.379 --> 00:25:08.292
Black bean noodles are the best!

241
00:25:15.681 --> 00:25:18.469
Bro? Where'd you go last night?

242
00:25:20.561 --> 00:25:21.722
Last night?

243
00:25:24.857 --> 00:25:27.474
You went out last night.

244
00:25:30.237 --> 00:25:31.898
No, I didn't go out.

245
00:25:33.824 --> 00:25:37.192
But I heard you go out the front door.

246
00:25:42.916 --> 00:25:47.410
You must've dreamt it.
You were tossing in your sleep.

247
00:25:51.425 --> 00:25:52.460
Did I?

248
00:25:53.510 --> 00:25:55.046
I'd better go.

249
00:25:55.345 --> 00:25:56.335
- Finished?
- Yup.

250
00:25:57.389 --> 00:26:01.223
- Clean this up, okay?
- Fine.

251
00:26:01.560 --> 00:26:03.221
- See ya.
- Bye!

252
00:26:09.902 --> 00:26:10.937
Bro?

253
00:26:12.196 --> 00:26:13.231
Yeah?

254
00:26:13.489 --> 00:26:15.400
What's with your leg?

255
00:26:18.243 --> 00:26:19.324
What?

256
00:26:19.661 --> 00:26:21.527
Why limp your right leg?

257
00:26:26.085 --> 00:26:27.075
I did?

258
00:26:27.169 --> 00:26:28.375
Yes, just now.

259
00:26:34.635 --> 00:26:38.754
Excuse me, but I'm running late.
Please don't joke, sir.

260
00:27:07.709 --> 00:27:08.824
You're home.

261
00:27:08.919 --> 00:27:10.205
- Hi, son.
- Hi, dad.

262
00:27:10.838 --> 00:27:13.455
Eat some veggies, not just meat.

263
00:27:13.632 --> 00:27:17.466
- After the ribs!
- Eat your veggies.

264
00:27:18.637 --> 00:27:20.548
- Hello.

265
00:27:21.265 --> 00:27:23.506
- Didn't eat, right?
- I'm starving.

266
00:27:23.934 --> 00:27:26.221
- Ribs?
- They're good.

267
00:27:30.899 --> 00:27:32.481
Hey!

268
00:27:32.568 --> 00:27:34.809
- Slept well?
- I didn't sleep.

269
00:27:34.945 --> 00:27:36.936
- Yes, you did.
- No, I didn't.

270
00:27:39.032 --> 00:27:41.023
I'm going to bed.

271
00:27:44.621 --> 00:27:47.613
Lie down. Don't sleep there.

272
00:27:48.292 --> 00:27:51.580
Go to sleep.
And I wasn't sleeping!

273
00:27:53.297 --> 00:27:54.412
Goodnight.

274
00:30:27.451 --> 00:30:28.236
Hello.

275
00:30:28.410 --> 00:30:30.196
Hurry! Follow that cab, please.

276
00:30:30.203 --> 00:30:31.693
- What?
- That taxi!

277
00:30:31.705 --> 00:30:32.820
Don't lose it!

278
00:32:23.483 --> 00:32:24.814
Hello, boss.

279
00:32:25.026 --> 00:32:26.312
Go inside.

280
00:32:27.362 --> 00:32:28.852
You bastards.

281
00:32:30.449 --> 00:32:32.110
Do your jobs right!

282
00:32:32.367 --> 00:32:33.698
I'm sorry, boss.

283
00:32:34.911 --> 00:32:36.822
- How many?
- Two.

284
00:32:37.581 --> 00:32:41.290
It's enough that things got fucked up!

285
00:32:42.586 --> 00:32:44.293
You could've seen wrong.

286
00:32:44.588 --> 00:32:46.795
There was no black van.

287
00:32:46.965 --> 00:32:47.955
Yes, sir.

288
00:32:49.301 --> 00:32:51.508
Can't you deal with
the damn officers?

289
00:32:54.306 --> 00:32:55.512
Listen up.

290
00:34:02.290 --> 00:34:03.906
Son of a bitch.

291
00:34:04.417 --> 00:34:06.829
Why come here and make trouble?

292
00:34:08.171 --> 00:34:09.286
Well...

293
00:34:10.382 --> 00:34:11.588
I can explain.

294
00:34:11.675 --> 00:34:13.666
What the fuck!

295
00:34:14.302 --> 00:34:17.465
When boss put so much into this...

296
00:34:17.472 --> 00:34:20.260
Wait. I can explain.

297
00:34:26.106 --> 00:34:26.686
Bastard!

298
00:34:26.690 --> 00:34:28.476
Get him!

299
00:34:28.900 --> 00:34:29.765
Hey!

300
00:34:29.859 --> 00:34:30.894
Fuck!

301
00:34:35.532 --> 00:34:36.488
Stop!

302
00:35:29.919 --> 00:35:30.875
Where'd he go?

303
00:35:30.962 --> 00:35:32.578
We're fucked!

304
00:35:33.173 --> 00:35:34.663
But he came this way.

305
00:35:34.966 --> 00:35:37.333
Fuck! He's gotta be around here.

306
00:35:43.016 --> 00:35:44.006
Hey!

307
00:35:44.601 --> 00:35:47.059
You go that way. I'll go this way.

308
00:36:49.582 --> 00:36:50.788
Studied all night?

309
00:36:55.088 --> 00:36:56.169
What's wrong?

310
00:36:59.467 --> 00:37:00.628
Why?

311
00:37:00.844 --> 00:37:03.882
You're jumpy. Is something wrong?

312
00:37:06.474 --> 00:37:09.967
No. It's nothing.

313
00:37:12.522 --> 00:37:13.853
Jin-seok!

314
00:37:25.493 --> 00:37:26.574
Jin-seok?

315
00:37:28.580 --> 00:37:30.036
What's going on?

316
00:37:31.166 --> 00:37:32.452
Are you okay?

317
00:37:33.418 --> 00:37:34.579
Jin-seok?

318
00:37:35.295 --> 00:37:36.535
Come on.

319
00:37:38.256 --> 00:37:40.247
Open the door.

320
00:37:41.384 --> 00:37:42.374
Please?

321
00:37:42.635 --> 00:37:44.091
Open the door.

322
00:37:44.304 --> 00:37:45.794
- Jin-seok...
- Get lost!

323
00:37:49.434 --> 00:37:54.144
Fine, I'll go. But tell
me why you're doing this.

324
00:37:54.981 --> 00:37:58.599
I followed you out last night!

325
00:37:58.860 --> 00:38:01.602
Followed me? Where?

326
00:38:01.821 --> 00:38:05.109
You know I fell asleep
as soon as I came in.

327
00:38:05.283 --> 00:38:06.694
I saw everything!

328
00:38:07.035 --> 00:38:10.073
Who were those men? They're not cops!

329
00:38:10.580 --> 00:38:13.948
Cops? Who are you talking about?

330
00:38:13.958 --> 00:38:16.120
The men who chased me!

331
00:38:21.966 --> 00:38:27.382
Did you have a bad dream again?

332
00:38:27.388 --> 00:38:28.719
Shut up!

333
00:38:30.517 --> 00:38:35.227
It wasn't a dream!
I remember it clearly!

334
00:38:36.231 --> 00:38:37.767
Thought I was sleeping?

335
00:38:38.233 --> 00:38:41.442
Well, I was until I heard
the pencil clicks!

336
00:38:42.237 --> 00:38:43.944
What pencil clicks?

337
00:38:44.030 --> 00:38:46.567
You clicked till the lead dropped!

338
00:38:51.204 --> 00:38:52.535
Where's my brother!

339
00:38:55.250 --> 00:38:57.241
What did you do to my brother!

340
00:39:00.129 --> 00:39:01.210
Say it!

341
00:39:46.050 --> 00:39:46.585
Let go!

342
00:39:46.593 --> 00:39:48.049
- Put it down.
- Let go!

343
00:39:48.052 --> 00:39:49.167
Stop!

344
00:39:52.390 --> 00:39:54.222
- Let go!
- Wait a sec.

345
00:39:54.559 --> 00:39:57.472
- Calm down!
- Let go of me!

346
00:39:57.562 --> 00:39:59.223
Calm down!

347
00:39:59.272 --> 00:40:01.263
Calm down, Jin-seok!

348
00:40:01.524 --> 00:40:04.186
- Let go!
- Calm down!

349
00:40:04.193 --> 00:40:05.228
Let go!

350
00:40:05.236 --> 00:40:07.273
Jin-seok! Calm down.

351
00:40:07.572 --> 00:40:08.687
You can't fool me!

352
00:40:08.698 --> 00:40:10.609
Calm down, Jin-seok!

353
00:40:10.909 --> 00:40:14.573
I swear I didn't go out
anywhere last night.

354
00:40:14.829 --> 00:40:18.447
But I saw you! What about those men!

355
00:40:18.625 --> 00:40:20.457
Calm down and listen to me.

356
00:40:20.543 --> 00:40:23.752
It's not real, okay?

357
00:40:24.005 --> 00:40:27.043
The pencil, the cab, the
men who chased you.

358
00:40:27.050 --> 00:40:29.587
They were all a dream!

359
00:40:31.888 --> 00:40:37.099
But I remember them clearly!
How do you explain that?

360
00:40:37.101 --> 00:40:38.341
Jin-seok!

361
00:40:39.103 --> 00:40:42.471
Did you take your pill?

362
00:40:42.732 --> 00:40:44.222
Yesterday?

363
00:40:48.947 --> 00:40:50.233
What are you doing?

364
00:40:51.157 --> 00:40:53.319
It's nothing.

365
00:41:01.125 --> 00:41:02.911
You didn't, did you?

366
00:41:26.442 --> 00:41:27.307
Bro?

367
00:41:34.367 --> 00:41:35.482
I'm sorry.

368
00:41:37.870 --> 00:41:39.452
Mom will be back soon.

369
00:41:40.164 --> 00:41:41.154
Rest up.

370
00:41:43.376 --> 00:41:44.366
Okay.

371
00:42:21.414 --> 00:42:22.449
Hello?

372
00:42:41.225 --> 00:42:42.932
I'm on my way now.

373
00:42:50.318 --> 00:42:55.108
The cab, the men who chased you!
They were all a dream!

374
00:42:57.658 --> 00:42:59.649
I didn't mention a cab.

375
00:43:04.248 --> 00:43:06.535
Jin-seok? I'm home.

376
00:43:07.502 --> 00:43:08.537
Mom!

377
00:43:10.296 --> 00:43:10.876
Yes?

378
00:43:13.633 --> 00:43:14.748
What's up?

379
00:43:18.471 --> 00:43:21.304
About Yu-seok...

380
00:43:25.436 --> 00:43:26.471
You mean...

381
00:43:28.731 --> 00:43:31.439
That really happened?

382
00:43:31.818 --> 00:43:34.310
It's the truth. I know it.

383
00:43:34.445 --> 00:43:37.187
I'd better talk to your dad.

384
00:43:37.240 --> 00:43:39.402
No, Mom. Not yet.

385
00:43:40.034 --> 00:43:42.492
- But your dad should...
- No, Mom!

386
00:43:42.995 --> 00:43:48.035
If he goes out again,
let's follow him with Dad.

387
00:43:55.675 --> 00:43:57.211
Yu-seok...

388
00:43:58.678 --> 00:44:02.012
Your brother really did that?

389
00:44:04.058 --> 00:44:07.141
He's not my brother.

390
00:46:11.519 --> 00:46:14.978
I called many times. Come quick.
There's a problem.

391
00:46:17.608 --> 00:46:20.191
The bastard is on to you.

392
00:46:24.407 --> 00:46:25.488
Yes.

393
00:46:31.038 --> 00:46:32.153
Right.

394
00:46:34.750 --> 00:46:35.615
Okay.

395
00:46:43.718 --> 00:46:47.382
He said that Yu-seok
was not his brother.

396
00:46:49.390 --> 00:46:53.304
Then he said he tailed you last night.

397
00:46:54.979 --> 00:46:58.222
He said your leg was fine
and the cops were fake.

398
00:46:58.816 --> 00:47:00.682
But when he woke up, he was home.

399
00:47:01.777 --> 00:47:03.688
That's what he told me.

400
00:47:04.405 --> 00:47:07.488
Yes! He said that! And...

401
00:47:13.039 --> 00:47:13.870
Yes.

402
00:47:14.707 --> 00:47:15.697
Okay.

403
00:47:16.876 --> 00:47:18.867
I know.

404
00:47:21.714 --> 00:47:22.704
Right.

405
00:47:25.760 --> 00:47:27.046
So I think...

406
00:47:35.436 --> 00:47:36.847
Who's there?

407
00:47:39.690 --> 00:47:40.805
Jin-seok?

408
00:47:47.907 --> 00:47:49.648
Is anyone here?

409
00:48:01.754 --> 00:48:04.462
No, I clearly heard something.

410
00:48:05.549 --> 00:48:07.290
Did he come down?

411
00:48:07.885 --> 00:48:10.377
No, he's fast asleep.

412
00:48:11.931 --> 00:48:13.717
I checked earlier.

413
00:48:14.392 --> 00:48:16.804
Okay, I'll go to his room.

414
00:49:31.802 --> 00:49:33.008
Mr. Park?

415
00:49:33.596 --> 00:49:35.678
What's taking you so long?

416
00:49:42.563 --> 00:49:44.554
Know what's going on here?

417
00:49:44.940 --> 00:49:45.805
Hurry!

418
00:49:45.816 --> 00:49:47.477
CHOI is on his way too.

419
00:51:02.601 --> 00:51:03.762
You're up?

420
00:51:18.742 --> 00:51:22.030
You sweat a lot.

421
00:51:23.914 --> 00:51:25.154
Way too much.

422
00:51:51.692 --> 00:51:54.059
Get here now.

423
00:51:56.030 --> 00:51:59.068
He's on to me too.

424
00:52:39.865 --> 00:52:41.947
Where are you going, son?

425
00:52:45.037 --> 00:52:46.027
Dad.

426
00:52:47.790 --> 00:52:49.406
Are you going somewhere?

427
00:52:55.714 --> 00:52:57.330
To meet a friend.

428
00:52:57.883 --> 00:53:00.215
Oh, really?

429
00:53:02.179 --> 00:53:02.884
Yes.

430
00:53:02.888 --> 00:53:04.219
What friend?

431
00:53:09.061 --> 00:53:11.223
Who are you going to meet?

432
00:53:13.273 --> 00:53:15.264
You don't know him. I'll be back soon.

433
00:53:16.819 --> 00:53:18.105
Jin-seok?

434
00:53:20.781 --> 00:53:22.442
You can't go.

435
00:53:31.542 --> 00:53:32.657
Let's go in.

436
00:53:34.002 --> 00:53:35.663
Let's go inside and talk.

437
00:53:37.464 --> 00:53:39.046
Let's go!

438
00:53:41.719 --> 00:53:42.675
Get him!

439
00:53:44.054 --> 00:53:45.260
Don't lose him!

440
00:54:41.779 --> 00:54:42.644
Help me!

441
00:54:42.780 --> 00:54:43.986
Please help me!

442
00:54:44.239 --> 00:54:45.479
What's with him?

443
00:54:53.373 --> 00:54:55.330
State your names.

444
00:54:56.752 --> 00:54:58.038
Yeon Jae-hyung.

445
00:54:58.045 --> 00:54:59.456
Yeon Jae-hyung?

446
00:55:02.299 --> 00:55:06.543
Let me get this straight.

447
00:55:07.679 --> 00:55:08.965
Some people

448
00:55:08.972 --> 00:55:13.341
locked you up for a month
and you just escaped?

449
00:55:13.811 --> 00:55:15.142
Yes, sir.

450
00:55:15.979 --> 00:55:18.266
You were locked up
in the big house up there?

451
00:55:19.358 --> 00:55:22.271
They pretended to be your family?

452
00:55:22.736 --> 00:55:23.942
That's right.

453
00:55:24.112 --> 00:55:27.275
So you thought they were your family?

454
00:55:27.366 --> 00:55:28.356
Is that it?

455
00:55:29.201 --> 00:55:31.192
Yes, that's what I thought.

456
00:55:32.287 --> 00:55:33.698
How were you tricked?

457
00:55:34.081 --> 00:55:37.119
How can anyone fool you
into being your family?

458
00:55:37.417 --> 00:55:39.408
That's what I don't get.

459
00:55:39.795 --> 00:55:43.629
I don't know how I was tricked.

460
00:55:44.049 --> 00:55:45.255
All right, then.

461
00:55:45.968 --> 00:55:47.333
Got the results on his ID?

462
00:55:47.845 --> 00:55:50.007
Yes, a while ago, sir.

463
00:55:50.305 --> 00:55:52.512
Why didn't you bring it sooner!

464
00:55:53.225 --> 00:55:54.841
- Sorry, sir.
- Give it to me.

465
00:55:56.311 --> 00:55:57.267
Got anything?

466
00:55:58.021 --> 00:56:03.858
Born April 27th, 1977, right?

467
00:56:04.278 --> 00:56:05.484
Yes, that's right.

468
00:56:05.571 --> 00:56:08.939
No one reported you missing.

469
00:56:09.199 --> 00:56:10.405
No crime either.

470
00:56:12.077 --> 00:56:14.944
So you're 40 years old, right?

471
00:56:16.498 --> 00:56:19.240
What? I'm 20 years old.

472
00:56:20.627 --> 00:56:25.292
Look, mister. How
could you be just 20?

473
00:56:25.632 --> 00:56:29.045
It's 1997, so I'm 20 years old.

474
00:56:34.349 --> 00:56:35.384
Mister.

475
00:56:36.184 --> 00:56:38.721
See the calendar over there?

476
00:56:41.356 --> 00:56:44.439
It's May, 2017.

477
00:56:53.368 --> 00:56:58.829
The poor man...

478
00:57:11.845 --> 00:57:15.554
Turn the TV on.
It's time for the news.

479
00:57:15.641 --> 00:57:16.722
Yes, sir.

480
00:57:18.185 --> 00:57:26.185
<i>President Moon was received
as if on a state visit to the U.S.</i>

481
00:57:26.985 --> 00:57:34.358
<i>President Trump held a banquet
and gave a tour of the White House.</i>

482
00:57:34.785 --> 00:57:37.117
<i>JUNG reports from Washington.</i>

483
00:57:37.412 --> 00:57:45.412
<i>Joint army-navy-air force guards
welcomed President Moon.</i>

484
00:59:08.795 --> 00:59:10.251
Come out!

485
00:59:10.547 --> 00:59:12.163
We need to talk.

486
01:00:39.094 --> 01:00:41.506
What is this?

487
01:00:44.683 --> 01:00:46.594
It didn't work.

488
01:01:08.707 --> 01:01:10.493
Who are you people?

489
01:01:11.376 --> 01:01:12.787
That's all you ask?

490
01:01:14.504 --> 01:01:16.666
Must be curious about many things.

491
01:01:18.133 --> 01:01:19.248
Tell me.

492
01:01:19.968 --> 01:01:21.709
What did you do to me?

493
01:01:32.981 --> 01:01:35.188
20 years ago,

494
01:01:35.567 --> 01:01:38.525
on December 20th, 1997,

495
01:01:40.488 --> 01:01:44.652
a family was murdered
in the outskirts of Seoul.

496
01:01:45.911 --> 01:01:47.743
In this very room.

497
01:01:52.000 --> 01:01:53.161
Working hard?

498
01:01:56.296 --> 01:01:57.411
What happened?

499
01:01:57.505 --> 01:01:58.370
Hi, sir.

500
01:01:58.924 --> 01:02:00.005
Oh my.

501
01:02:00.759 --> 01:02:05.378
<i>A mother and daughter were
brutally stabbed to death.</i>

502
01:02:15.106 --> 01:02:17.313
<i>It was all over the media.</i>

503
01:02:17.776 --> 01:02:21.610
<i>Even a special investigative
team was put to the case.</i>

504
01:02:23.114 --> 01:02:25.355
<i>But cops couldn't catch the killer.</i>

505
01:02:28.119 --> 01:02:30.531
<i>One year, two years...</i>

506
01:02:32.666 --> 01:02:37.627
<i>As time passed, people
started to forget about it.</i>

507
01:02:38.588 --> 01:02:42.627
<i>It was completely forgotten when
the statute of limitations ended.</i>

508
01:02:43.718 --> 01:02:44.708
<i>But</i>

509
01:02:45.595 --> 01:02:47.677
<i>the victims' family
could never forget.</i>

510
01:02:50.892 --> 01:02:54.010
<i>They hired people to solve the case.</i>

511
01:02:56.147 --> 01:02:57.262
<i>A month passed...</i>

512
01:02:57.691 --> 01:02:58.556
<i>then two months...</i>

513
01:02:58.650 --> 01:02:59.856
<i>Seasons passed.</i>

514
01:03:01.611 --> 01:03:04.228
<i>On a spring day 4 years later...</i>

515
01:03:08.493 --> 01:03:10.450
<i>We finally found the killer.</i>

516
01:03:12.038 --> 01:03:13.278
Why'd you do it?

517
01:03:15.083 --> 01:03:17.245
You didn't know them at all.

518
01:03:18.003 --> 01:03:20.165
I don't remember anything!

519
01:03:20.755 --> 01:03:22.462
You don't remember?

520
01:03:22.841 --> 01:03:23.672
No.

521
01:03:36.938 --> 01:03:37.928
Kill him.

522
01:03:45.238 --> 01:03:47.855
<i>You're saying I'm the killer?</i>

523
01:03:48.325 --> 01:03:50.316
<i>Yes, you.</i>

524
01:03:50.702 --> 01:03:51.658
No.

525
01:03:52.829 --> 01:03:54.319
There's no way.

526
01:03:56.082 --> 01:03:59.791
I know I didn't kill anyone.

527
01:03:59.794 --> 01:04:03.253
The bastard keeps denying it.

528
01:04:04.716 --> 01:04:07.128
<i>He's definitely the killer,</i>

529
01:04:08.720 --> 01:04:10.802
<i>but he claimed he's innocent.</i>

530
01:04:12.766 --> 01:04:14.348
<i>I could sense it.</i>

531
01:04:15.643 --> 01:04:17.680
<i>It didn't seem like he was lying.</i>

532
01:04:18.271 --> 01:04:21.639
<i>The victims' family
was totally taken aback.</i>

533
01:04:22.734 --> 01:04:24.725
<i>Something was not right.</i>

534
01:04:25.278 --> 01:04:28.691
<i>They found the bastard
who destroyed their lives.</i>

535
01:04:29.157 --> 01:04:32.866
<i>They want revenge, but the
killer can't remember.</i>

536
01:04:34.579 --> 01:04:38.493
<i>Whether he did it alone
or had an accomplice,</i>

537
01:04:38.500 --> 01:04:40.787
<i>or if someone ordered him to it...</i>

538
01:04:41.878 --> 01:04:45.496
<i>They can't kill him
when he can't remember.</i>

539
01:04:47.008 --> 01:04:49.670
<i>So we brought in another expert.</i>

540
01:04:50.220 --> 01:04:53.258
<i>A former expert in
hypnotic investigations.</i>

541
01:04:54.057 --> 01:04:55.718
I'm PARK Sung-dae.

542
01:04:56.393 --> 01:04:59.431
Let's say this is
SONG Jin-seok's life.

543
01:04:59.813 --> 01:05:05.650
Divide it into childhood, teens,
twenties, thirties, and forties.

544
01:05:08.071 --> 01:05:09.607
Why can't you open it?

545
01:05:09.823 --> 01:05:11.154
I don't know.

546
01:05:11.908 --> 01:05:13.069
Around this time,

547
01:05:13.159 --> 01:05:15.742
SONG experienced something horrific

548
01:05:15.995 --> 01:05:18.327
<i>and erased the memory himself.</i>

549
01:05:18.415 --> 01:05:20.156
Can you try?

550
01:05:20.417 --> 01:05:24.752
<i>We tried everything to
revive the erased memory.</i>

551
01:05:25.380 --> 01:05:29.544
But he is suppressing it so hard.

552
01:05:31.052 --> 01:05:32.759
<i>We were right.</i>

553
01:05:33.847 --> 01:05:35.838
<i>He couldn't remember.</i>

554
01:05:37.434 --> 01:05:39.892
<i>He had dissociative amnesia.</i>

555
01:05:40.770 --> 01:05:43.228
<i>The most painful memories...</i>

556
01:05:44.023 --> 01:05:48.233
<i>The bastard wiped them off himself.</i>

557
01:05:48.778 --> 01:05:52.737
Right before SONG was
involved in the case,

558
01:05:53.324 --> 01:05:56.191
we must go back before tragedy hit.

559
01:05:57.120 --> 01:06:00.238
- To when he was happy?
- Right.

560
01:06:00.498 --> 01:06:02.580
Before May 6, 1997.

561
01:06:03.793 --> 01:06:08.708
<i>Make him take Barbital.
It's a hypnotic agent.</i>

562
01:06:08.798 --> 01:06:10.835
What an honor.

563
01:06:10.967 --> 01:06:14.210
Why come and see little, old me?

564
01:06:19.267 --> 01:06:21.429
I heard you did some acting.

565
01:06:21.853 --> 01:06:25.346
<i>Think of it as a kind of role play.</i>

566
01:06:26.566 --> 01:06:31.811
We'll hypnotize him to think
he's traveling on a train.

567
01:06:32.655 --> 01:06:37.240
As he goes through each
tunnel on the way,

568
01:06:37.243 --> 01:06:42.704
he'll go back a year to a
happier time in his life.

569
01:06:43.625 --> 01:06:46.743
Then, let's begin.

570
01:06:47.212 --> 01:06:51.297
Let's go into the first tunnel.

571
01:06:52.050 --> 01:06:55.839
Now, you're out of the tunnel.

572
01:06:56.638 --> 01:06:58.220
What year is it now?

573
01:07:01.976 --> 01:07:03.967
What year is it?

574
01:07:11.236 --> 01:07:12.897
I'll ask again.

575
01:07:13.821 --> 01:07:15.687
What year is it?

576
01:07:28.878 --> 01:07:31.870
19...

577
01:07:33.049 --> 01:07:34.881
97.

578
01:07:42.976 --> 01:07:44.967
How old are you?

579
01:07:46.354 --> 01:07:47.890
Twenty.

580
01:07:48.314 --> 01:07:49.679
Good.

581
01:07:50.692 --> 01:07:52.683
Where are you now?

582
01:07:54.070 --> 01:07:55.435
In a car.

583
01:07:55.780 --> 01:07:56.815
A car?

584
01:07:57.949 --> 01:08:00.111
Headed where with whom?

585
01:08:02.287 --> 01:08:03.573
<i>My mom...</i>

586
01:08:04.372 --> 01:08:05.737
<i>My dad...</i>

587
01:08:07.166 --> 01:08:08.702
<i>My older brother...</i>

588
01:08:09.127 --> 01:08:11.414
<i>We're moving to our new house.</i>

589
01:08:11.963 --> 01:08:14.796
What are you doing in the car?

590
01:08:15.592 --> 01:08:19.051
<i>Resting on my mom and taking a nap.</i>

591
01:08:20.096 --> 01:08:27.560
When I give you the order,
you'll wake up from that nap.

592
01:08:28.980 --> 01:08:30.186
Yes.

593
01:08:30.815 --> 01:08:32.806
<i>When you wake up,</i>

594
01:08:33.109 --> 01:08:36.397
<i>you'll still be 20 years old.</i>

595
01:08:37.280 --> 01:08:40.318
<i>It's the year 1997.</i>

596
01:08:41.993 --> 01:08:44.985
<i>The people in the car with you</i>

597
01:08:45.997 --> 01:08:52.585
<i>are your father, mother,
and older brother.</i>

598
01:08:54.631 --> 01:08:56.588
Now!

599
01:08:57.008 --> 01:08:58.919
When I count to three,

600
01:08:59.093 --> 01:09:01.209
you'll wake up from the nap.

601
01:09:02.555 --> 01:09:03.420
One...

602
01:09:05.183 --> 01:09:06.173
Two...

603
01:09:07.810 --> 01:09:08.800
Three!

604
01:09:13.316 --> 01:09:16.604
Why are you sweating?

605
01:09:16.819 --> 01:09:18.560
Are you okay?

606
01:09:19.781 --> 01:09:20.771
Mom?

607
01:09:21.658 --> 01:09:22.568
Yes, Jin-seok.

608
01:09:24.369 --> 01:09:26.736
<i>That strangely familiar house...</i>

609
01:09:28.164 --> 01:09:33.034
<i>It's where you killed two
people 20 years ago.</i>

610
01:09:34.003 --> 01:09:36.711
<i>Of course, it felt familiar.</i>

611
01:09:36.923 --> 01:09:37.788
Are you okay?

612
01:09:37.882 --> 01:09:40.169
That man is your older brother?

613
01:09:40.468 --> 01:09:41.299
We don't look alike.

614
01:09:41.469 --> 01:09:44.052
Then how old is your brother?

615
01:09:45.890 --> 01:09:46.504
Why?

616
01:09:46.516 --> 01:09:47.722
Mister?

617
01:09:52.939 --> 01:09:54.100
What's that sound?

618
01:09:57.193 --> 01:09:58.604
Wasn't it the thunder?

619
01:09:58.611 --> 01:10:01.854
- We're really lucky.
- I know.

620
01:10:05.660 --> 01:10:07.150
The fuck!

621
01:10:14.752 --> 01:10:18.120
Okay, okay. Going for
a walk should help.

622
01:10:19.257 --> 01:10:24.093
<i>We had some close calls, but
everything was going to plan.</i>

623
01:10:27.473 --> 01:10:30.886
<i>To bring back a killer's memory
of that late, rainy night,</i>

624
01:10:31.602 --> 01:10:33.593
<i>we set the house exactly as it was.</i>

625
01:10:37.066 --> 01:10:42.277
<i>We even had the music set to
play just like 20 years ago.</i>

626
01:10:43.489 --> 01:10:45.856
<i>MR. PARK</i>

627
01:10:48.745 --> 01:10:50.076
Dad?

628
01:10:51.205 --> 01:10:52.240
That was Dad?

629
01:10:53.416 --> 01:10:54.406
Wait here.

630
01:10:54.417 --> 01:10:59.503
<i>The only thing left was the killer
to walk into the house as planned.</i>

631
01:11:02.258 --> 01:11:04.716
<i>But something unexpected happened.</i>

632
01:11:05.470 --> 01:11:06.460
Police.

633
01:11:07.430 --> 01:11:09.216
You're under arrest for fraud.

634
01:11:09.557 --> 01:11:12.640
<i>Cops found me right then of all times.</i>

635
01:11:12.977 --> 01:11:13.967
Bro!

636
01:11:14.228 --> 01:11:18.517
<i>Everything could've been ruined
when they arrested me.</i>

637
01:11:18.524 --> 01:11:19.685
Yu-seok's been abducted!

638
01:11:19.692 --> 01:11:24.061
<i>Thankfully, you thought
I was abducted.</i>

639
01:11:24.322 --> 01:11:26.154
Jin-seok! Wake up!

640
01:11:29.243 --> 01:11:30.278
What the hell?

641
01:11:30.328 --> 01:11:32.820
Abducted? Call CHOI now!

642
01:11:34.332 --> 01:11:35.163
What's going on?

643
01:11:37.376 --> 01:11:41.370
<i>I paid and pulled strings,
then got out in 19 days.</i>

644
01:11:42.006 --> 01:11:45.089
<i>We wanted to get on with the play.</i>

645
01:11:46.719 --> 01:11:49.336
<i>But fuck! It didn't rain.</i>

646
01:11:50.807 --> 01:11:53.219
<i>It had to be on a rainy night.</i>

647
01:11:54.227 --> 01:11:59.813
<i>You started to slip out of
hypnosis, and got suspicious.</i>

648
01:11:59.816 --> 01:12:01.306
The bastard's on my tail.

649
01:12:04.278 --> 01:12:07.316
He said your leg was fine
and the cops were fake.

650
01:12:07.323 --> 01:12:13.160
<i>Your suspicions eventually
led you to here.</i>

651
01:12:20.753 --> 01:12:21.914
Get it now?

652
01:12:23.506 --> 01:12:25.167
Why we did it?

653
01:12:25.174 --> 01:12:26.539
And why you're here?

654
01:12:30.221 --> 01:12:31.211
What?

655
01:12:33.391 --> 01:12:34.802
Think I'm lying?

656
01:12:35.393 --> 01:12:36.383
No.

657
01:12:38.187 --> 01:12:39.848
It's probably true.

658
01:12:40.064 --> 01:12:41.395
Except one thing.

659
01:12:41.399 --> 01:12:42.230
What?

660
01:12:44.151 --> 01:12:45.266
I didn't do it.

661
01:12:46.571 --> 01:12:48.107
I never killed anyone.

662
01:12:48.114 --> 01:12:50.151
You fucking bastard!

663
01:12:52.034 --> 01:12:53.945
You killed them.

664
01:12:54.287 --> 01:12:56.198
And you'll be dead soon.

665
01:12:56.289 --> 01:12:58.872
In the most painful way there is.

666
01:12:59.584 --> 01:13:00.574
No.

667
01:13:02.253 --> 01:13:04.665
I'm not dying.

668
01:13:10.469 --> 01:13:11.379
Fuck!

669
01:13:18.269 --> 01:13:19.475
Son of a bitch!

670
01:13:20.897 --> 01:13:21.637
Turn around!

671
01:13:24.317 --> 01:13:25.648
Turn around now!

672
01:13:30.281 --> 01:13:33.023
Where did that bastard go!

673
01:13:39.081 --> 01:13:39.866
Faster!

674
01:13:41.250 --> 01:13:42.035
Step on it!

675
01:13:52.303 --> 01:13:53.384
Over there!

676
01:13:57.892 --> 01:13:58.472
Hey!

677
01:14:03.481 --> 01:14:04.721
Stop! Stop!

678
01:14:08.611 --> 01:14:09.942
What the fuck!

679
01:14:11.322 --> 01:14:12.733
Move the car!

680
01:14:41.727 --> 01:14:42.717
Shit!

681
01:16:37.301 --> 01:16:40.259
Are you okay, sir?

682
01:16:41.263 --> 01:16:42.253
Oh shit!

683
01:16:46.894 --> 01:16:51.479
911? There's been an accident.

684
01:16:52.900 --> 01:16:55.608
A man just jumped into the street.

685
01:17:04.787 --> 01:17:06.118
He's breathing.

686
01:17:06.122 --> 01:17:08.705
- Blood pressure is normal.
- Check his vitals.

687
01:17:09.500 --> 01:17:10.661
Can you hear me?

688
01:17:13.129 --> 01:17:14.665
Do you know where this is?

689
01:17:33.482 --> 01:17:36.349
<i>MAY, 1997</i>

690
01:17:48.664 --> 01:17:49.904
Jin-seok!

691
01:17:51.292 --> 01:17:52.453
Jin-seok!

692
01:17:54.920 --> 01:17:55.625
Bro!

693
01:17:55.629 --> 01:17:57.290
The car is fixed!

694
01:17:58.340 --> 01:18:01.924
Jin-seok! Let's go! Hurry!

695
01:18:03.387 --> 01:18:05.094
Coming, Mom!

696
01:18:07.099 --> 01:18:09.932
Remember my friend Jin-san?

697
01:18:10.186 --> 01:18:12.052
The chicken shop's son?

698
01:18:12.062 --> 01:18:13.052
Yes.

699
01:18:13.063 --> 01:18:14.519
How's he doing?

700
01:18:14.523 --> 01:18:15.638
He's getting married.

701
01:18:15.649 --> 01:18:17.481
- Really?
- Yes.

702
01:18:20.654 --> 01:18:21.860
Jin-seok?

703
01:18:22.281 --> 01:18:24.739
Must be tired. Lean on me and sleep.

704
01:18:25.826 --> 01:18:28.238
He must've dated for a long time.

705
01:18:28.954 --> 01:18:30.945
His fiancé is pregnant.

706
01:18:31.207 --> 01:18:32.618
- Really?
- Yes.

707
01:18:34.919 --> 01:18:36.910
Do you have a girlfriend?

708
01:18:37.296 --> 01:18:38.286
No.

709
01:18:50.476 --> 01:18:52.467
<i>6 MONTHS LATER</i>

710
01:18:52.519 --> 01:18:54.681
<i>Dear citizens.</i>

711
01:18:55.189 --> 01:19:00.434
<i>Our economy is in great
turmoil at present.</i>

712
01:19:02.154 --> 01:19:04.646
<i>Stemming from Southeast
Asian countries,</i>

713
01:19:05.532 --> 01:19:10.698
<i>the financial market crisis
combined with our economic problems</i>

714
01:19:11.413 --> 01:19:13.575
<i>is amplifying the crisis.</i>

715
01:19:14.166 --> 01:19:19.332
<i>After 30 years of strong
economic progress</i>

716
01:19:19.672 --> 01:19:22.835
<i>that the world envied,</i>

717
01:19:31.016 --> 01:19:33.599
<i>FAST PRIVATE LOANS</i>

718
01:19:35.813 --> 01:19:37.019
No way in hell!

719
01:19:37.022 --> 01:19:38.638
Please, sir! Help me.

720
01:19:39.608 --> 01:19:40.689
Just once.

721
01:19:43.028 --> 01:19:43.859
Scram!

722
01:19:44.071 --> 01:19:45.232
I'm a high school graduate.

723
01:19:45.239 --> 01:19:46.695
I'll do anything.

724
01:19:46.699 --> 01:19:48.235
I'm really sorry.

725
01:19:48.242 --> 01:19:52.827
But could you pay me for
a few months up front?

726
01:20:06.468 --> 01:20:10.382
<i>HEALTHY 20 YEAR-OLD IN DIRE NEED OF MONEY
My older brother is very sick.</i>

727
01:20:13.809 --> 01:20:18.303
<i>IF YOU PAY ME UP FRONT,
I'LL BE INDEBTED FOR LIFE.</i>

728
01:20:28.866 --> 01:20:30.527
Hi, doctor.

729
01:20:34.872 --> 01:20:41.710
Your parents passed away and
your brother's been sick for months.

730
01:20:43.756 --> 01:20:46.748
As his doctor, I feel terrible.

731
01:20:48.844 --> 01:20:51.051
I'm sorry to say this,

732
01:20:52.348 --> 01:20:53.804
but there's no time.

733
01:20:54.767 --> 01:20:57.885
He needs surgery as soon as possible.

734
01:20:59.313 --> 01:21:00.803
Or else we can't save him.

735
01:21:03.859 --> 01:21:04.940
I understand.

736
01:21:14.912 --> 01:21:16.368
Come to your senses!

737
01:21:16.372 --> 01:21:18.659
Know how scary that is?

738
01:21:19.875 --> 01:21:21.161
Organ donating?

739
01:21:21.168 --> 01:21:25.708
It's done by quacks.
You'll die soon after it.

740
01:21:25.923 --> 01:21:27.379
Many folks even die during it.

741
01:21:27.800 --> 01:21:29.757
I know you're strapped for cash,

742
01:21:29.760 --> 01:21:32.673
but don't do it. The economy crashed.

743
01:21:32.971 --> 01:21:36.180
<i>Just stay low and wait it out.</i>

744
01:21:47.611 --> 01:21:49.818
<i>BLUE BEARD WANTS TO CHAT.
WILL YOU ACCEPT?</i>

745
01:21:52.991 --> 01:21:55.198
<i>DID YOU MEAN WHAT YOU WROTE?</i>

746
01:21:59.873 --> 01:22:02.786
<i>YES, I'LL DO ANYTHING FOR MONEY.</i>

747
01:22:02.793 --> 01:22:05.285
<i>EVEN GIVE UP YOUR SOUL?</i>

748
01:22:06.547 --> 01:22:07.537
What?

749
01:22:12.219 --> 01:22:14.506
<i>WHY DO YOU ASK THAT?</i>

750
01:22:14.513 --> 01:22:16.003
<i>YOU NEED MONEY.</i>

751
01:22:16.014 --> 01:22:18.927
<i>AND I NEED YOUR DESPERATENESS.</i>

752
01:22:21.186 --> 01:22:23.974
<i>HOW MUCH WILL IT TAKE?</i>

753
01:22:28.068 --> 01:22:30.776
<i>TELL ME THE JOB FIRST TO...</i>

754
01:22:34.783 --> 01:22:37.775
<i>FOR THE PRICE TO KILL.</i>

755
01:22:39.413 --> 01:22:42.246
<i>FOR THE PRICE TO KILL.</i>

756
01:22:46.628 --> 01:22:52.419
<i>YOU HAVE TILL NOON TOMORROW.
SEND YOUR NUMBER, IF YOU'LL DO IT.</i>

757
01:22:57.139 --> 01:22:59.847
<i>IF PAST NOON, YOUR CHANCE IS GONE.</i>

758
01:23:10.486 --> 01:23:13.604
- Let's go!
- Wait up!

759
01:23:30.881 --> 01:23:33.873
<i>SEND THE MESSAGE?</i>

760
01:23:50.108 --> 01:23:51.223
Hello?

761
01:23:52.110 --> 01:23:56.445
<i>Write down the address I give you.</i>

762
01:23:59.117 --> 01:24:04.908
<i>425 Seong-shin-dong,
Seongseo-gu, Seoul.</i>

763
01:24:11.880 --> 01:24:13.871
<i>There are 3 people inside.</i>

764
01:24:15.008 --> 01:24:17.215
<i>A woman and two children.</i>

765
01:24:19.972 --> 01:24:23.931
<i>Don't touch the kids.
Just kill the woman.</i>

766
01:24:25.352 --> 01:24:29.971
<i>Remember! Just the woman.</i>

767
01:25:20.324 --> 01:25:22.406
You're home?

768
01:25:25.078 --> 01:25:26.159
Honey?

769
01:25:28.957 --> 01:25:29.947
Dear?

770
01:25:41.720 --> 01:25:43.051
Don't scream, please.

771
01:25:43.388 --> 01:25:44.674
I'll just go.

772
01:25:46.391 --> 01:25:47.631
Please don't scream.

773
01:25:54.650 --> 01:25:58.063
I'm sorry. I must've
been out of my mind.

774
01:25:59.112 --> 01:26:00.318
- I'm sorry.
- Mom?

775
01:26:00.572 --> 01:26:01.858
Is Daddy home?

776
01:26:08.538 --> 01:26:09.118
No!

777
01:26:09.498 --> 01:26:12.240
Don't scream!

778
01:26:13.627 --> 01:26:14.833
Stop screaming!

779
01:26:16.004 --> 01:26:16.994
Don't scream!

780
01:26:17.005 --> 01:26:17.870
No!

781
01:26:21.259 --> 01:26:22.249
Wait!

782
01:26:28.475 --> 01:26:30.011
Don't scream, please.

783
01:26:30.686 --> 01:26:32.097
I'll just go.

784
01:26:34.022 --> 01:26:36.434
I said stop screaming!

785
01:27:32.789 --> 01:27:38.956
I asked you not to scream.

786
01:27:41.089 --> 01:27:42.045
I'm sorry!

787
01:27:45.135 --> 01:27:47.126
I told you not to scream!

788
01:27:48.013 --> 01:27:51.506
Why didn't you listen to me!

789
01:27:51.683 --> 01:27:53.265
Chan-mi!

790
01:27:55.228 --> 01:27:57.094
Don't scream!

791
01:29:22.524 --> 01:29:23.514
Mister?

792
01:29:34.661 --> 01:29:36.402
Who are you?

793
01:29:38.540 --> 01:29:40.531
Where's my mom?

794
01:29:54.723 --> 01:29:56.134
Listen to me.

795
01:29:57.017 --> 01:30:04.606
If you do as I say, I'll
bring your mom and sister.

796
01:30:05.233 --> 01:30:06.394
Really?

797
01:30:09.362 --> 01:30:12.946
Go put the blanket over yourself.

798
01:30:14.242 --> 01:30:18.406
Then count to a hundred ten times.

799
01:30:18.830 --> 01:30:19.820
Got it?

800
01:30:20.916 --> 01:30:21.906
Okay.

801
01:30:34.429 --> 01:30:40.095
One, two, three, four...

802
01:30:41.311 --> 01:30:44.224
Five, six...

803
01:30:55.075 --> 01:30:56.065
Hello?

804
01:30:56.409 --> 01:31:00.824
<i>Write down the address I give you.</i>

805
01:31:01.831 --> 01:31:06.371
Seong-shin-dong,
Seongseo-gu, Seoul.

806
01:31:07.629 --> 01:31:09.745
<i>There are 3 people inside.</i>

807
01:31:10.632 --> 01:31:12.919
<i>A woman, two children.</i>

808
01:31:14.010 --> 01:31:17.799
<i>Don't touch the kids.
Just kill the woman.</i>

809
01:31:18.723 --> 01:31:22.557
Ninety-eight,
ninety-nine, one hundred!

810
01:31:23.478 --> 01:31:25.970
One, two...

811
01:31:26.481 --> 01:31:28.768
<i>Three, four...</i>

812
01:31:29.859 --> 01:31:32.817
<i>Five, six...</i>

813
01:31:42.205 --> 01:31:43.161
Hello?

814
01:31:43.999 --> 01:31:45.455
<i>Daddy!</i>

815
01:31:45.709 --> 01:31:48.041
Sung-wook? What's wrong?

816
01:31:48.670 --> 01:31:52.004
I did what the man said.

817
01:31:52.507 --> 01:31:56.091
I counted to a hundred ten times.

818
01:31:56.344 --> 01:32:00.212
But mom and Chan-mi
are bleeding on the floor.

819
01:32:00.557 --> 01:32:01.592
What happened to Chan-mi?

820
01:32:02.392 --> 01:32:04.099
They're not breathing.

821
01:32:04.477 --> 01:32:06.309
Okay, I'll be right there.

822
01:32:20.952 --> 01:32:22.033
Doctor?

823
01:32:22.537 --> 01:32:23.618
Why?

824
01:32:25.957 --> 01:32:27.243
But she's family.

825
01:32:28.251 --> 01:32:29.867
With her sacrifice,

826
01:32:31.212 --> 01:32:33.499
we won't have to live in the streets.

827
01:32:35.508 --> 01:32:37.465
I need her insurance money.

828
01:32:38.428 --> 01:32:40.715
How could you do that to your family?

829
01:32:41.973 --> 01:32:43.964
You did it to save your brother!

830
01:32:44.392 --> 01:32:46.383
I did it to save my kids!

831
01:32:47.645 --> 01:32:50.933
But you ruined everything!

832
01:32:52.609 --> 01:32:56.477
My daughter is dead and
your brother will die too!

833
01:32:59.240 --> 01:33:02.483
Now, it's your turn!

834
01:33:12.420 --> 01:33:14.252
Doctor? Why me?

835
01:33:15.173 --> 01:33:16.208
No reason!

836
01:33:16.800 --> 01:33:18.461
Just die!

837
01:33:28.061 --> 01:33:29.051
Doctor!

838
01:33:29.562 --> 01:33:30.802
No!

839
01:33:31.564 --> 01:33:33.305
No!

840
01:34:33.376 --> 01:34:35.538
Life's a bitch, huh?

841
01:34:46.181 --> 01:34:47.546
Had enough?

842
01:34:54.355 --> 01:34:55.595
I'm sick of it too.

843
01:34:58.484 --> 01:34:59.599
I'll end it for you.

844
01:35:16.461 --> 01:35:18.623
Where's the victims' family?

845
01:35:19.547 --> 01:35:20.537
Why?

846
01:35:23.760 --> 01:35:26.297
I deserve to die.

847
01:35:28.139 --> 01:35:31.006
Please tell them that.

848
01:35:43.988 --> 01:35:45.570
Your memory is back?

849
01:35:54.582 --> 01:35:58.701
For what? Why'd you kill those two?

850
01:36:04.259 --> 01:36:05.966
Someone put you to it?

851
01:36:11.641 --> 01:36:12.847
By chance...

852
01:36:13.768 --> 01:36:15.759
Was it the woman's husband?

853
01:36:20.275 --> 01:36:22.482
I found out recently

854
01:36:24.362 --> 01:36:30.608
that he took out hefty
insurance in the woman's name.

855
01:36:31.661 --> 01:36:32.651
Tell me.

856
01:36:34.372 --> 01:36:37.785
Did he order the kill
for the insurance?

857
01:36:43.798 --> 01:36:48.008
The victims' family wants to know.

858
01:36:50.930 --> 01:36:53.968
The kid you didn't kill that night...

859
01:36:54.309 --> 01:36:55.720
The little boy...

860
01:36:58.521 --> 01:37:02.105
Tell him the truth
and beg forgiveness.

861
01:37:04.402 --> 01:37:08.987
You said you'll bring Mom if I
count to a hundred ten times.

862
01:37:12.660 --> 01:37:14.901
Know how I lived after that?

863
01:37:15.705 --> 01:37:17.946
My cousins took all the money.

864
01:37:17.957 --> 01:37:19.994
I was sent to an orphanage.

865
01:37:21.669 --> 01:37:24.878
I cried every night and vowed

866
01:37:25.798 --> 01:37:32.761
to find the man who killed
my family when I grow up.

867
01:37:34.557 --> 01:37:36.673
Find him and get revenge!

868
01:37:37.852 --> 01:37:41.470
Fuck! Why didn't you kill
that boy then too?

869
01:37:41.689 --> 01:37:42.679
Huh?

870
01:37:44.901 --> 01:37:47.689
Should've killed the boy, you fucker!

871
01:37:51.074 --> 01:37:52.280
I'm sorry.

872
01:37:55.828 --> 01:37:56.784
I apologize.

873
01:37:58.081 --> 01:37:59.412
I'm so sorry.

874
01:38:02.377 --> 01:38:03.492
I'm sorry.

875
01:38:05.713 --> 01:38:06.578
I'm sorry.

876
01:38:08.341 --> 01:38:09.547
Fuck!

877
01:38:17.809 --> 01:38:18.924
Now, tell me.

878
01:38:22.522 --> 01:38:24.229
Did the husband order it?

879
01:38:26.109 --> 01:38:27.099
Tell me!

880
01:38:27.819 --> 01:38:29.810
Did my dad order it?

881
01:38:38.496 --> 01:38:39.486
No.

882
01:38:41.249 --> 01:38:42.739
It was just me.

883
01:38:45.420 --> 01:38:46.535
I did it.

884
01:38:48.047 --> 01:38:49.162
Just me.

885
01:38:56.180 --> 01:38:58.171
Shit.

886
01:39:01.394 --> 01:39:02.930
I knew it.

887
01:39:07.191 --> 01:39:09.853
The husband taking
out the insurance...

888
01:39:12.238 --> 01:39:15.947
It was a coincidence, right?

889
01:39:28.337 --> 01:39:29.372
Fuck.

890
01:39:32.008 --> 01:39:35.251
You expect me to believe that?

891
01:39:56.616 --> 01:39:57.731
Have a good life.

892
01:40:49.210 --> 01:40:50.621
Excuse me, sir?

893
01:40:50.878 --> 01:40:52.744
There's no way out that way.

894
01:40:53.047 --> 01:40:55.334
The elevators are this way.

895
01:42:40.154 --> 01:42:44.944
<i>FORGOTTEN</i>

896
01:42:46.744 --> 01:42:48.109
Jin-seok!

897
01:42:48.621 --> 01:42:49.986
The car is fixed!

898
01:42:50.748 --> 01:42:54.366
Jin-seok! Let's go! Hurry!

899
01:42:55.211 --> 01:42:57.168
Coming, Mom!

900
01:43:05.262 --> 01:43:06.377
Hi.

901
01:43:07.390 --> 01:43:08.471
How old are you?

902
01:43:10.142 --> 01:43:11.678
You're five?

903
01:43:16.399 --> 01:43:18.390
No, thanks. It's okay.

904
01:43:20.236 --> 01:43:22.568
Sung-wook!

905
01:43:23.114 --> 01:43:24.275
Mommy!

906
01:43:32.081 --> 01:43:33.913
What did that nice man say?

907
01:43:36.460 --> 01:43:37.950
Wanna go on rides?

908
01:43:37.962 --> 01:43:39.452
Let's go, Sung-wook.

909
01:43:39.922 --> 01:43:41.037
High five!

910
01:43:59.150 --> 01:44:02.734
<i>KANG Ha-neul</i>

911
01:44:03.738 --> 01:44:07.106
<i>KIM Moo-yeul</i>

912
01:44:08.159 --> 01:44:11.697
<i>MOON Seong-geun, NA Young-hee</i>

913
01:44:12.621 --> 01:44:16.080
<i>a JANG Hang-joon film</i>
